+# Workspace notes
+
+Tutorial-owned resource. Members read and create notes through the web guard;
+REST/MCP use the same permissions through the operation catalog. Capabilities
+trust verified `WorkspaceContext`, never a caller-supplied Workspace ID.
+
+- Seed and Live create a note and its audit event. Live commits both in one D1 batch.
+- Notes contain 1–500 characters. Transport boundaries decode the shared payload.
+- Lists use the shared newest-first keyset cursor and always filter by Workspace ID.
+- The web page shows the latest 30 notes; REST/MCP support pagination.
+- This tutorial does not add paid entitlements or provider dependencies.
